# Jaguar XJ (XJ40/X300/X308), 1986-2003.
#
# The XJ40 of October 1986, heavily revised as the X300 in 1994 and re-engined as
# the X308 in 1997; one body family with four circular headlamps in pairs, a low
# roofline and a sloping tail. 2.9-4.0 six, 6.0 V12, then 3.2/4.0 V8; 5,024 mm
# long, 1,799 mm wide, 1,314 mm high, wheelbase 2,870 mm. The largest class-4
# parc of the 1990s: 87,374 XJ40/X300/X308 licensed in 1995.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_XJ_(XJ40)
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_XJ_(X300)
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_XJ_(X308)
#
# Colours: black, British Racing Green, sapphire blue and silver are period
# Jaguar finishes. The modelled form follows the X300/X308.
#
# Weight: 60 in total (black 20, green 15, blue 15, silver 10) against the
# 1989-2025 Very-high gap. Provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 180 km/h; comfort 150/555 (line).
# Dates: 1986-2003, with a road tail to the mid-2010s.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-xj.blend. References:
# citycars/references/jaguar-xj/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

